  "_doc": "The fifteen functional roles (content_bible.md 9.2; builtin_ai.md 4.2 and 4.3): per role a behavior tree (node ids prefixed with the role, unique across roles) and the role actions its act leaves name. cond and guard arguments are predicate names of src/systems/npc/brain/predicates.ts joined by AND, a leading ! negates; say arguments are line slots; durations are game time (30m, 12h, 1d). A role action's weight is its utility in the duty layer's usel; `do` is the activity, a schedule place ('@here' stays, '@player' walks up to the player, '@patient' goes to the one being treated), a note id and an effect of src/systems/npc/brain/role_effects.ts.",
